.TH CSTR_DESTROY 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_destroy \- destroy a cstr and set it to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_destroy(s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro is a type-inferred alias for cstring_destroy(). It destroys the
string and sets the pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   cstr lvalue to destroy, such as a variable or an element of an
    array. The macro evaluates it exactly once, and sets it to NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
A call with a NULL pointer is safe, and it does nothing
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_destroy (3)
